# Index-First Context Strategy
- **Consult the Map First:** Before reading source code, inspect `PROJECT_GRAPH.md` at the project root to locate the exact module, function, or interface. Never blindly grep or dump multiple full files into the context window.
- **Surgical Loading:** Read ONLY the specific file and line ranges identified in `PROJECT_GRAPH.md`.

# Graph Maintenance Rules
- **Keep it Synchronized:** When adding, deleting, moving, or modifying exports, routes, models, or core functions, update `PROJECT_GRAPH.md` in the same turn.
- **Ultra-Dense Format:** The graph must remain compact and machine-readable (symbol names, single-line descriptions, call relationships). Do not write narrative essays or include implementation details.

# Output & Token Thrift
- **Diffs Only:** Output only the code lines that change. Use `// ... existing code ...` to preserve unmodified lines.
- **Zero Explanations:** Provide no pleasantries, setup statements, or recap summaries. Emit the code fix or command directly.